      "prompt": "Walk me through a time you had to diagnose and fix a slow-running query in a high-traffic PostgreSQL database. What tools did you use to identify the bottleneck, and how did you validate that your changes improved performance without compromising data integrity?",
      "answer_outline": "The candidate should mention using EXPLAIN ANALYZE to inspect query plans, identifying issues like sequential scans or missing indexes. They should discuss the trade-offs of adding indexes versus rewriting queries, and mention verifying results using staging data or production-like load testing.",
      "difficulty": 3
